    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** leads the charge with an elite 84.82 score. Facing Griffin Canning and his 4.76 xERA, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a massive SP skill boost and a favorable platoon matchup, making him our primary engine for runs and stolen bases. Close behind, **Seiya Suzuki** (73.90) is positioned for a monster outing; he draws a rare home park factor surge (+16%) against Triston Rogers. While **Brice Turang** holds a strong 63.01, he warrants close attention; despite his high SB potential against Pallante, there is a 38% risk of rain that could shorten his afternoon or disrupt his rhythm on the basepaths.\n\nThe bench decision process was particularly tight at the middle infield slots. **Jose Caballero** just missed the cut with a 39.32, falling agonizingly short of our 40-point \"Zebras Floor.\" While his speed remains a weapon, he was suppressed by a poor matchup against Rasmussen, whose 3.33 xERA stifled the projection. Conversely, **Mickey Moniak** managed to secure a spot in the lineup at 62.32 despite a negative platoon adjustment, as his favorable spot in the order and the wind-aided conditions in his park provided enough upside to justify the start over the contact-focused bench options.\n\nManagement remains cautious regarding our \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Kyle Karros**, **Corbin Carroll**, and **Mickey Moniak**. While we have projected them based on historical trends, any deviation in the batting order\u2014specifically for **Mickey Moniak** or **Gabriel Moreno**\u2014could shift their utility scores significantly. We are keeping **Edwin Arroyo** on standby, though he remains firmly benched today due to a tough draw against Luzardo, leaving us with a balanced, speed-heavy lineup designed to extract maximum value from today\u2019s favorable pitching matchups.",
